                <pb facs="0646" n="576" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg576"/>

                <head>No. 23.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#center">[Telegram.—From <placeName>San Luis
                            Potosi</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-06-02">June 2,
                            1867</date>, at 10.45 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>To General <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mariano Escobedo</hi> :</p>
                <p>About 10 to-night I received a telegraphic despatch from you with the
                    recommendation of General Diaz to notify him of what is done in relation to the
                    petition of Baron Magnus. The President being indisposed has retired, so I
                    cannot consult him till to-morrow, when I will give you an answer.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. LERDO DE TEJADA.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
